{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Skipping per workflow after second plan-review failure. Verbatim blocking findings from retry: E4 — The plan's fix ('Change the residue's minuend ONLY to apparent size' while 'Leave docker_storage_bytes on ALLOCATED blocks') assumes the two are separable, but in the code both are the SAME single value: docker_total_bytes = DOCKER_DU_TOTAL from one census walk that feeds docker_storage_bytes and the residue subtraction. G1G2/T3/G6 — the plan must specify how to obtain both allocated blocks for docker_storage_bytes and apparent size for residue without a second Docker-root du walk, because a single du invocation reports one size semantic and a second walk reintroduces bug 9313's timeout regression. Required resolution: revise plan to name the mechanism (or explicitly accept/update the single-walk budget/tests) before claim/implementation."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788832372482716001,"uuid":"0ce9eafd-9f07-4d43-8589-091593e78c18"}